---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const email = 'clement.cazaud@outlook.com';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How poesis.cloud and docs.poesis.cloud handle personal data — what is collected, why, and your rights."
  pageType="Legal"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container legal-doc">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-note">Last updated: 2026-08-16.</p>
      <p>
        This policy covers poesis.cloud and docs.poesis.cloud (together, "the
        sites").
      </p>

      <h2>Data controller</h2>
      <p>
        The data controller is Poesis (company registration pending — see the
        <a href="/legal/mentions-legales">legal notice</a>), reachable at
        <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Website analytics (Google Analytics 4).</strong> Only if you
          accept analytics cookies: we collect pseudonymous usage data (pages
          visited, approximate location derived from a truncated IP address,
          device and browser information). IP anonymization is enabled. If you
          reject analytics cookies, the Google Analytics script is not loaded and
          no analytics data is collected.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Contact.</strong> If you email us, we process your email address
          and message content to respond to you.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The sites have no contact forms, no accounts, and no newsletters — no
        other personal data is collected through the sites themselves.
      </p>

      <h2>Purpose and legal basis</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Analytics:</strong> understanding how the sites are used, to
          improve them. Legal basis: your consent (which you can withdraw at any
          time via "Cookie settings" in the footer).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Responding to emails:</strong> handling your request. Legal
          basis: our legitimate interest in answering professional enquiries, and
          pre-contractual steps where relevant.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Processors and international transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Analytics data is processed by Google Ireland Limited / Google LLC. This
        involves a transfer to the United States, covered by the EU–US Data
        Privacy Framework.
      </p>
      <p>
        The sites are hosted by GitHub, Inc. (United States), also under the
        EU–US Data Privacy Framework.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention</h2>
      <p>
        Google Analytics data is retained for 14 months. Emails are kept as long
        as needed to handle the exchange, then deleted or archived per our
        internal retention practices.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You have the right to access, rectify, erase, restrict, or object to the
        processing of your personal data, and the right to data portability. To
        exercise these rights, contact
        <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. You also have the right to lodge
        a complaint with the CNIL (<a href="https://www.cnil.fr" target="_blank" rel="noopener">cnil.fr</a>).
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        See the <a href="/legal/cookies">cookie policy</a> for the list of cookies
        used and how to manage your consent.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
